Candidates will have unparalleled learning opportunities for learning and accelerated career growth working in a fast-paced, hyper-growth startup environment. As a member of the team, you’ll have opportunities to:

• Salary ranges from 1,500 to 3,000 USD per month based on experience and interview results;
• 100% salary social insurance;
• Quarterly, yearly, 13-month bonus;
• Annual health check, company trip and other company’s activities;
• Develop core competencies in the areas of technology and computer science;
• Take on high-impact and ultra-challenging projects that push the technological frontier of the company;
• Flexible/hybrid work environment.

- Chế độ BHXH theo cấp bậc và thâm niên công tác;
- Tài trợ 100% thẻ BHSK Bảo Việt cho NLĐ và con đầu tiên, 70% cho con thứ 2,... khám tại tất cả các BV Công và Quốc tế;
- Khám sức khỏe định kỳ 01 lần/năm tại Bệnh viện dịch vụ 5 sao.

Tiện ích văn phòng:
- Không gian làm việc đầy đủ tiện nghi (văn phòng làm việc xanh, tủ lạnh, lò vi sóng..; siêu thị, nhà hàng, bể bơi, gym, bi-a, hair salon, trường mầm non ngay bên cạnh).
- Cơm văn phòng tự chọn.

Đào tạo:
- Đào tạo nội bộ, đào tạo ngoài kiến thức chuyên môn, kỹ năng... phục vụ công việc.

Các hoạt động sôi nổi:
- Du xuân, du lịch hè, family day 3 lần/năm;
- Cấp quỹ Entertainment 100k/người/tháng theo team/phòng ban;
- Tổ chức sinh nhật cho CBNV định kỳ 01 lần/tháng;
- Câu lạc bộ, giải bóng đá, bóng bàn, cầu lông, bi-a, esport,...
Thời gian làm việc: Từ T2 - hết thứ 6, thứ 7 làm việc/ nghỉ cách tuần.

Are you driven by a passion for shaping the future of AI-powered products and thrive in a collaborative, fast-paced, and innovation-focused environment? At Renn Labs, we believe in the power of technology to transform industries, and we’re looking for Senior Product Associates to help us take our AI solutions to the next level. Join a dynamic team where your insights and creativity will directly contribute to building groundbreaking products that redefine the market. This isn’t just another job - it’s your chance to make a lasting impact while working with a team that values collaboration, excellence, and cutting-edge thinking.

THE IMPACT YOU'LL MAKE IN THIS ROLE

- Comprehensively conducting detailed market and competitor research to identify emerging trends and inform product strategy;
- Diligently conducting planned testing and experimentation to optimize product features and improve user experiences;
- Thoughtfully uncovering actionable insights by analyzing user behavior, product performance, and key metrics using analytics tools;
- Precisely translating defined business needs into technical requirements for development teams, bridging the gap between all stakeholders;
- Efficiently facilitating conducted requirement-gathering sessions and creating detailed documentation such as user stories, process flows, and acceptance criteria;
- Fruitfully collaborating with teams to design and optimize thoroughly processes, ensuring they align with product capabilities;

- Rigorously conducting product roadmap by facilitating operations, tracking progress, validating that solutions meet business and user expectations, and helping to maintain clear communication across teams;
- Closely track key product performance metrics, gather user feedback and project metrics, using this data to recommend process improvements and product adjustments;
- Compellingly presenting findings and recommendations through crafted reports, dashboards, and visualizations to drive informed decision-making;
- Meticulously collaborating with Product Managers to define and maintain a data-driven roadmap, prioritizing features that deliver maximum value to users, identifying bottlenecks, risks, and blockers in the product lifecycle, working to resolve them and improve efficiency;
- Dynamically staying at the forefront of evolving industry trends and emerging technologies, incorporating best practices into product and business strategies;
- Constantly fostering a culture of creativity, collaboration, adaptability, persistence, a results-driven focus, high standards for deliverables, and continuous improvement within the Software team and throughout the entire company.

WHAT YOU’LL NEED TO MAXIMIZE IMPACT IN THIS ROLE

- Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Business, Data Analytics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.

- Above 3 years of experience working as Product Analyst, Business Analyst, Product Owner, Project Coordinator, Product Operations etc.; The designated title will be assigned based on your strengths, experience, and potential for growth.
- Experience gathering, analyzing, researching, documenting, and translate business needs into technical solutions;
- Knowledge of UX design principles and one or many tools such as Figma, InVision, Adobe XD, Balsamiq etc.;
- Proficiency with analytics tools (e.g., Google Analytics, SQL, Tableau, PowerBI etc.) and A/B testing methods;
- Experience working in Agile frameworks and familiarity with product collaboration tools;
